-- title:
--   Level-Nt roof field generated by X₁(Nt) and q↦ q^t
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $N$, $t$, $q$ be nonzero natural numbers, and let $N'$ be a natural number with $N' = Nt$. All fields occurring are intermediate fields of the Laurent series field $L((q))$, respectively $\mathbb{Q}((q))$; for an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) denotes the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, and [`ModularCurve.qExpand L t`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) is the ring endomorphism of $L((q))$ obtained by multiplying all Hahn-series exponents by $t$, i.e. the substitution $q \mapsto q^{t}$. Here [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField N'`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) is the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma1 N')` of ratios of $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma_1(N')$, and [`ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M s`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L142) is the analogous subfield for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(s)$. The assertion is the equality of intermediate fields of $L((q))$: the join of the base change to $L$ of the $\Gamma_1(N')$-field with the subfield generated over $L$ by the image under $q \mapsto q^{t}$ of the base change to $L$ of the $\Gamma_1(N) \cap \Gamma_0(Nq)$-field equals the base change to $L$ of the $\Gamma_1(N') \cap \Gamma_0(N'q)$-field.
--
--   This is the statement that the $q$-expansion function field of the "roof" curve $X(\Gamma_1(Nt) \cap \Gamma_0(Ntq))$ is generated over that of $X_1(Nt)$ by the pull-back along $\tau \mapsto t\tau$ (substitution $q \mapsto q^{t}$) of the function field of the level-$N$ roof $X(\Gamma_1(N) \cap \Gamma_0(Nq))$, after base change of coefficients to $L$. It is used in the verification that the degeneracy pull-back maps commute with the Hecke operators, in [`ModularCurve.JOne.degeneracyPullbackPair_comm_heckeOperatorOneBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JOne.degeneracyPullbackPair_comm_heckeOperatorOneBar).
